# Test: daemon start refuses retired selector values (netlink, nft, tc) before any plugin starts, and ze doctor reports them.
# Question: does `ze start` on a file holding `interface backend netlink`,
#           `firewall backend nft`, and `traffic control backend tc` exit 1
#           before any plugin starts with all three joined refusals and
#           `set <selector> kernel` fixes, and does `ze doctor` report them
#           under `doctor-dataplane-mismatch`?
#           A unit test checks `LoadConfig` and doctor separately; only the
#           real daemon start and doctor CLI prove both surfaces refuse all
#           three retired values end to end.
# VALIDATES: spec-dataplane-compatibility-guard AC-19 (N-1, F-4 proof) --
#            retired backend names refuse daemon start before any plugin
#            starts and appear under `doctor-dataplane-mismatch` in `ze doctor`.
# PREVENTS: any residual alias allowing `netlink`, `nft`, or `tc` to boot or
#           escaping `ze doctor`.

tmpfs=retired.conf:refused=config-plugin-verify:terminator=EOF_CONF
interface {
	backend netlink;
}
firewall {
	backend nft;
}
traffic {
	control {
		backend tc;
	}
}
EOF_CONF

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze start retired.conf:timeout=30s
expect=exit:code=1
expect=stderr:contains=error: load config:
expect=stderr:contains=interface backend "netlink"
expect=stderr:contains=set interface backend kernel
expect=stderr:contains=firewall backend "nft"
expect=stderr:contains=set firewall backend kernel
expect=stderr:contains=traffic control backend "tc"
expect=stderr:contains=set traffic control backend kernel
reject=stderr:contains=interface backend loaded
reject=stderr:pattern=panic

cmd=foreground:seq=2:exec=ze doctor --json config retired.conf:exit=1:timeout=20s
expect=stdout:contains=doctor-dataplane-mismatch
expect=stdout:contains=interface backend \"netlink\"
expect=stdout:contains=firewall backend \"nft\"
expect=stdout:contains=traffic control backend \"tc\"
